{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"difficult-delightful-moray","creation_channel":"cli","description":"ProductionBatchRunner.run receives req.usd_budget as a per-plan cost cap override, but there is no clean seam in today's pass1/sizing API to apply it: run_pass1 → sizing.shed_to_budget computes the cap internally via sizing.plan_budget_cap(ctx) (reading REBAR_PLAN_REVIEW_BUDGET as the base, then centrality-scaling it), with no injection point. The only current overrides are (a) mutating the process-global, centrality-scaled env var (NOT a true cap override) or (b) adding a cap-override parameter — gate code outside the thin adapter. Today the requested override is JOURNALED (coverage.requested_usd_budget / budget_override_applied=false, a WARNING) and the computed cap is used. Follow-up: thread an explicit cap_override through run_pass1 → shed_to_budget so req.usd_budget is honoured. Discovered while triaging comments in src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py (ticket ad16).","id":"e907-8dbd-7627-4725","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"plan-review: explicit cap_override seam through run_pass1 -> shed_to_budget"},"env_id":"4d084713-8164-4b68-9afe-601bbda46966","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786186460877981001,"uuid":"4eed46a5-6305-4585-a38b-15ee49b10cfe"}